{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>I am a hundred and twenty years old today.</b> And there is no reason to grieve over my death, for I was no longer fit to live by nature." "<b>I can no longer go out and come in.</b> And even if I were alive, I would not be able to go out and come in before you in my old age." "<b>And HaShem said to me, You shall not cross over.</b> And even if I were able to go out and come in, HaShem said to me, You shall not cross over. And if so, it is better for you that I die, so that you will be able to cross over."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:43.003172481Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}